<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Scandinavia and the Baltic</p><h1 class="st-title">Latvian Socialist Soviet Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1918 CE – 1920 CE · capital Riga</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Bolshevik Latvia of 1918-1920, led by Pēteris Stučka, which briefly held Riga before being driven out in the Latvian War of Independence.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany's</a> defeat, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latvian-riflemen">Latvian Riflemen</a> invaded <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-latvia">Latvia</a>. On 17 December 1918 a Soviet government under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peteris-stucka">Pēteris Stučka</a> proclaimed the Latvian Socialist Soviet Republic, and on 3 January 1919 it took Riga, forcing the national government of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karlis-ulmanis">Kārlis Ulmanis</a> to retreat to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liepaja">Liepāja</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Soviet government nationalised land, industry and housing and created revolutionary tribunals, which carried out hundreds of executions. Food requisitioning caused famine in Riga. Its army controlled most of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-latvia">Latvia</a> in early 1919, and it adopted a constitution in January.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/freikorps">German Freikorps</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baltic-landeswehr">Baltic Landeswehr</a>, with Latvian national units, recaptured Riga on 22 May 1919. The Soviet government held on in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latgale">Latgale</a> until Latvian and Polish forces took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daugavpils">Daugavpils</a> in January 1920, and it was dissolved. The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-latvia">Republic of Latvia</a> signed peace with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/russian-sfsr">Soviet Russia</a> in August 1920.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/latvian-socialist-soviet-republic.jpg" alt="Latvian Socialist Soviet Republic" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Himasaram · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Latvian_Socialist_Soviet_Republic_(1918%E2%80%931920).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1918 CE – 1920 CE</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Riga</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Pēteris Stučka</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Latvian, Russian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Latvia</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Soviet Latvia 1918-1920, Latvijas Sociālistiskā Padomju Republika</dd></dl></aside></div>
